%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% View 2 — why there is no flag day.
%%
%% The naive path needs one synchronised commit across four repositories.
%% The taken path splits ENCAPSULATION (behaviour-preserving, incremental)
%% from REPRESENTATION (core-local once encapsulated).
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graph LR
    subgraph NAIVE["✗ naive — flag day"]
        N1["change Id in core"] --> N2["ALL 4 repos break<br/>at the same instant"]
        N2 --> N3["one synchronised commit<br/>coordinated revert<br/>196 sites at once"]
    end

    subgraph TAKEN["✓ taken — no flag day"]
        T1["M2a accessors<br/>additive, nothing breaks"]
        T2["M2b call sites<br/>one repo at a time<br/>every repo always compiles"]
        T3["M2c seal<br/>missed sites become<br/>COMPILE ERRORS, not<br/>silent wrong answers"]
        T4["M1 representation<br/>zero call sites touched"]
        T1 --> T2 --> T3 --> T4
    end

    classDef bad fill:#fdeaea,stroke:#a33,color:#4a1414
    classDef good fill:#e8f4ea,stroke:#2f6b3f,color:#12301c
    class N1,N2,N3 bad
    class T1,T2,T3,T4 good

%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% View 3 — transaction lifecycle (M4).
%%
%% Validation is where every failure lives, so commit is infallible and atomic
%% Batch falls out rather than being bolted on. The bindings map is what
%% today's `apply` cannot produce (audit §4.6) — the reason deltas are not
%% gossipable at all right now.
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle

    Idle --> Staging: Begin
    Staging --> Staging: delta → overlay<br/>(base IR untouched)
    Staging --> Validating: Commit
    Staging --> Idle: Abort — overlay dropped

    Validating --> Committing: all checks pass
    Validating --> Rejected: any check fails
    Rejected --> Idle: base IR never mutated

    Committing --> Committed: infallible write
    Committed --> Idle: receipt issued

    Idle --> Idle: exact replay (txn_digest match)
    Idle --> Conflict: same version, different txn_digest
    Conflict --> Idle: reported, never silently merged

    note right of Validating
        Local refs resolve · committed refs
        live (generation matches) · arc arity
        preconditions · no dangling created ·
        hierarchy acyclic · Ir::validate on
        the POST-state.
        Reuses M0.4 — one predicate, not two.
    end note

    note right of Committed
        Receipt carries:
          base/target version
          txn_digest   (identifies the CHANGE)
          state_digest (identifies the RESULT)
          bindings LocalId → DeclKey  ← §4.6
          cascaded removals
          axes_touched → §H invalidation
    end note

    note right of Conflict
        Needs BOTH version and digest.
        resuming_at() restores only the
        version today, so a resumed replica
        cannot tell legitimate replay from
        a fork. §G.3.
    end note
